Z||000003||Nashco||09-17-2001||07:26 AM||||I have a '69 VW bug that I drove for three years, that I'm now upgrading from a 1600 flat four to a 4.3 V6 with a '69 turbo porsche four speed.  I've got almost all the parts I need, now I just need to get away from school long enough to work on it!!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/brycenbug.jpg"> <P>It was in awesome shape when I got it, but the floorpans quickly deteriorated after taking it out of the desert.  I've got new floor pans and a new luggage tray I'm putting in, and considering a body lift while I'm at it.  It's my baby <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I just wish I had it with me instead of my fiero so I could fix it, rather than upgrade the fiero...sometimes <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||10
Z||000004||Formula88||09-17-2001||08:54 AM||||Well, in addition to my 88 Formula, my daily driver is a '99 Grand Am, 3400SFI V6.  I say it's my daily driver, but really, I drive the Fiero most of the time.  I usually only drive the GA to work, or when I'm working on the Fiero.  That 3400SFI V6 is a great little engine, and now that Magnuson has come out with a supercharger for it that puts it up to about 262 HP, there may be another engine swap option for Fieros!  I wonder how well my GA would run with the 2.8 outta my Fiero...  hmmmm.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
