Z||000032||Cheever3000||09-18-2001||12:06 AM||||Nashco, I love it.  I had a 68 that I put my sandbuggy motor in, which had been built up to 1835cc and tripled the h.p.  I then took the whole thing apart, turned it into a Baja, rewired it myself and built my own dash with Stewart Warner gauges.  Got a real strong clutch while I was at it.  Had it painted sorta like the Starsky car, but with dessert colors.  Converted the windows to one-piece.  Tried to use it for a daily driver, but the cam was too wild for the street and the muffler restricted it too much.  Besides, I got engaged.  So I sold it to buy the wedding rings.  Someday I might do it again, cause it was a LOT of fun working on & driving that car.  When I get a scanner, I'll post the pics.<BR>||||reg||1
